# Project Specifics
- Unless stated differently create all components as React components in src\business-apps folder
- Each component should extend its props from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.
- Whenever an access token is required, use it from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.
- Whenever an user, an user info or an employee ID is required, use it from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.
- Whenever a structure id is required, use it from the `BusinessAppContextProps` interface.

# Naming Conventions
- use kebab-case for folders (e.g. "src\business-apps\fin\expenses\personal-expenses"
- use PascalCase for files like apps, forms, and components (e.g. PersonalExpenses.tsx, EmployeeRecord.tsx)
- use camelCase for files like index.ts, hooks, utils, types, other functions, etc.

# Folder Structure for business apps
- folders in src\business-apps represent modules (e.g. hr, fin, crm etc.)
- folders in src\business-apps\<module> represent either sub-modules (e.g. core, absences, expenses, etc.) or shared resources for this module (e.g. `components`, `hooks`, `types`, `utils`, `queries`, etc.)
- folders in src\business-apps\<module>\<sub-module> represent either `apps` (e.g. personal-expenses, manager-expenses, employee-record, etc.), `forms` (e.g. expense-item-form, expense-request-form, etc.) or shared resources for this sub-module (e.g. `components`, `hooks`, `types`, `utils`, `queries`, etc.)
- files in src\business-apps\<module>\<sub-module>\apps\<app-name> are related to that single app where one `*.tsx` (PascalCase) with the name of app is located and an `index.ts` (camelCase) file with a named export of the component and a default export of the component.
- files in src\business-apps\<module>\<sub-module>\forms\<form-name> are related to that single app where one `*.tsx` (PascalCase) with the name of form is located and an `index.ts` (camelCase) file with a named export of the component and a default export of the component.

Folder Structure Examples for Apps and Forms:
- src\business-apps\hr\hr-core\apps\employee-directory\EmployeeDirectory.tsx
- src\business-apps\hr\hr-core\forms\employee-creation-form\EmployeeCreationForm.tsx

