# Component Dependencies
- Use react for UI components
- Use tailwind v4 for all styling (utility classes)
- Use ant-design for React UI components
- Use @dnd-kit for drag and drop
- Use zustand for state management in React
- Use react-dom for working with the DOM
- Use typescript for type safety
- Use prettier for code styling
- Use eslint for linting

- Do not install other packages for UI themes, icons, etc. unless absolutely necessary or I request them.
- The list of required dependencies must be small and simple and must reuse existing packages.

- For all date and time related logic, use `dayjs` and import the plugins `weekday` and `localeData`.

# Component Development
- Always prefix all CSS classes with the `gba:` prefix.
- Always add to all HTML elements in a component the `data-testid` attribute with a value which is unique and descriptive.

- Whenever an input field is used to provide search by an user, use the existing `DebouncedInput` component to provide debounced search.
- When tab components are used, provide a unique tab key for each tab and use this in a URL query parameter.

- Add all CSS files in `src/index.css`, so that they are included in `dist/assets/main.css` by the vite bundler. Only this way will they be applied on the NEWWORK platform.

- For Graphql API requests, use src\common\network\graphql\useGraphQLClient.ts
- For REST API requests, use src\common\network\rest\useRestClient.ts
- For all API requests to a service, check if already exists in src\common\network, or create a new folder for that service.

# Project Development
- Simplify the code as much as possible and keep it clean
- Remove unused code
- Remove commented code
- Use the Conventional Commits specification for git commit messages

# Publishing
- apps and forms need to be published on a daily basis
- apps: Use npm run publish:screen -- /<module>/<sub-module>/apps/<app-folder> to publish an app
- forms: Use npm run publish:screen -- /<module>/<sub-module>/forms/<form-folder> to publish a form
